adr: 0215
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: typeinquiry_access_errors
why: AP 6.4.9's containment is by construction: a bare name is put back in tqAt/tqLen, so a program of ISO/IEC 10206:1991 takes 6.4.9's own path and every rule the clause already had is asked the question it was written for. Sending a bare name down the access path instead looks harmless -- InquiryOfAccess answers the same type for `type of n` -- and it is not: the closest-containing rule, the schematic-formal refusal and the slice refusal are all written against tqAt/tqLen and stop being asked. Re-anchored after ADR-0232, which reindented the arm; the killer moved too, `dialect-containment` having compiled the conformance corpus a second way and gone with the modes.
--- old
          if obj^.kind = nkVar then begin
            t^.tqAt := obj^.vrAt;
            t^.tqLen := obj^.vrLen
          end
          else
            t^.tqObj := obj
--- new
          t^.tqObj := obj
